Calc keeps one '#' on XLSX hyperlinks whose location starts with '#'

The XLSX importer always put '#' before a hyperlink's location. Some
writers already store the location as "#'Sheet'!A1" (Ely R15.28,
issue #57), so the cell's URL became "##'Sheet'.A1"
and no jump could resolve it. The importer now adds '#' only when the
location lacks one.

diff --git a/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheethelper.cxx b/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheethelper.cxx
index 3b24f22a8..3d34b67b2 100644
--- a/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheethelper.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/filter/oox/worksheethelper.cxx
@@ -1005,8 +1005,9 @@ OUString WorksheetGlobals::getHyperlinkUrl( const HyperlinkModel& rHyperlink ) c
     OUStringBuffer aUrlBuffer;
     if( !rHyperlink.maTarget.isEmpty() )
         aUrlBuffer.append( getBaseFilter().getAbsoluteUrl( rHyperlink.maTarget ) );
+    // Some writers put the '#' in the location itself.
     if( !rHyperlink.maLocation.isEmpty() )
-        aUrlBuffer.append( "#" + rHyperlink.maLocation );
+        aUrlBuffer.append( rHyperlink.maLocation.startsWith( "#" ) ? rHyperlink.maLocation : "#" + rHyperlink.maLocation );
     OUString aUrl = aUrlBuffer.makeStringAndClear();
 
     if( aUrl.startsWith("#") )
